## Purpose

This file is the persistent context for AI-assisted work on the Event24 Web App.

It is the single source of truth for:

- current Web App architecture
- current module/page inventory
- mandatory frontend patterns
- backend API integration rules
- participant/organizer auth boundaries
- visual/UI preservation rules
- runtime/environment configuration
- known API contracts
- active mock-vs-real-data state
- recent changes and reasoning

Every meaningful code change must update this file.

A new agent should be able to read only `.agent` and correctly continue the project.

`AGENTS.md` is leftover Lovable copy and is not product truth. `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` is the standalone human briefing for marketers, stakeholders, and newcomers (what the product is, journeys, live features, brand language, what not to claim). `WORKSPACE_STATE.md` is the cross-agent stage/decision briefing. This `.agent` file remains the engineering source of truth. Leftover `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` files may still mention mock data.

## Project Identity

Event24 Web App is a standalone Vite + React + TypeScript SPA.

The repository originated from a Lovable-generated event application.

Lovable is now the visual/theme foundation only.

Its original backend, Supabase integration, product rules, entities, routes, and business logic are not authoritative for Event24.

The Laravel Event24 backend is a separate project and is authoritative for API contracts and domain behavior.

Local Laravel + Admin project (not modified by this Web App unless a prompt says so): `D:\Orbit Systems\EventHub\events-admin`

## Human briefing

`PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` (repo root) is the product context file for people, not agents. Hand it to marketers and newcomers. It covers positioning, the three experiences (house / event page / org console), attendee and organizer journeys, live feature map, Waafi/plans/payouts in plain language, locked CTAs, and explicit non-claims (no form builder, no waitlist, no Wallet, no live newsletter). Engineering contracts, routes, and API shapes stay in this file. Do not treat `README.md` as a substitute for either document.

