Update this table whenever module status/data source changes.

## Mandatory Frontend Patterns

### API

- all API requests through centralized clients/services
- never hardcode Laravel URLs
- never hardcode API keys
- never add HMAC
- never invent endpoint names
- verify non-public API contracts against current Laravel state before implementing

### UI

- preserve Lovable visual language
- reuse existing components first
- do not genericize the product
- mobile-first
- no UI regression during API wiring
- loading states for all real async requests
- error states for all real async requests

### TypeScript

- this repo currently has `strict: false` and `noImplicitAny: false` in `tsconfig.app.json`
- new Event24 API/domain types must still be explicit
- no unexplained any in new API code
- do not reintroduce mock fixtures as backend truth

### Data flow

Preferred:

API → service → hook/page → component

Avoid:

component → raw axios → backend

## Mock Data Policy

Production routes must not import mock fixtures. `src/lib/mockData.ts` was deleted.

Do not restore production mock dependencies or invent fake analytics/attendee series.

When adding screens: wire Laravel contracts or show honest empty/error/deferred UI — never silently mock production data.

## Deferred / Out of Core Scope (Prompt 14)

Do not build unless explicitly requested after Prompt 14:

- Apple/Google Wallet passes
- Push notifications
- Multi-language
- Native mobile apps
- Offline QR scanning
- Production deployment / production Waafi credentials
- Admin payout approve / reject / record-payment (admin panel)
- Organizer-wide batch payout create (per-event only in Web App)
- Richer email campaign tooling beyond announcements
- Certificate issuance (participant read-only when `available: false`)

## Organizer Package Self-Subscription (Web + Backend)

Laravel Prompt 15 + Web App checkout UI:

- Route `/organizer/subscription` (alias `/organizer/billing`) — Plans & billing
- Top nav: Dashboard, Events, Plans, Payouts, Settings
- Service `organizerPackages.ts`: list/subscribe/history/orders; POST body only `{ package_id, payer_phone? }`; subscribe timeout 190s
- UI: `SubscriptionQuotaPanel` + `PackageSubscribeDialog` (free activate / paid EVC phone); compact embed on Payouts → Package tab
- Catalog uses backend `selectable` / `upgrade_allowed` / `blocked_reason` (no client-side tier rules)
- Dashboard + event-create quota errors link to Plans

## Prompt 14 Quality Notes

- **API key 401:** `missing_api_key` / `invalid_api_key` → config error via `isApiKeyConfigErrorPayload`; never clear participant/organizer sessions
- **Session 401:** clears that role only → `/auth?expired=1` or `/organizer/login?expired=1`
- **Errors:** `getApiErrorMessage` covers network, 403, 404, 422, 5xx, domain codes; filters stack-like blobs; no raw server dumps in UI
- **Loading:** page skeletons / button busy / modal inline; avoid full-page spinner when shell can stay
- **Code splitting:** `React.lazy` for heavy/dashboard routes; scanner & analytics in separate chunks
- **Images:** catalog/list `loading="lazy"` + `decoding="async"`; standard `<img>`; no Next.js Image
- **a11y:** labels, focus, Escape on dialogs (Radix), scanner button names, `prefers-reduced-motion` CSS, Lenis reduced-motion (Lenis is not mounted on `/organizer`)
- **Security:** no HMAC, no Supabase, no secrets in repo, safe internal redirects only, event descriptions as text nodes (no unsanitized HTML renderer)

## Backend Contract Rule

The old Next.js Web App foundation/prompt pack is stale architecture.

In particular, do NOT reintroduce:

- Next.js
- server proxy routes
- HMAC API signatures
- Next.js env names
- guessed endpoint names

The current Laravel implementation is authoritative.

## Known Ownership Boundary

Admin = platform owner.

Organizer = owner/operator of their events.

Organizer-facing actions such as live Waafi charging and QR door validation must use organizer scope.

Do not allow Web App architecture to accidentally use admin-panel tokens.

## Known Risks / Watchouts

- VITE_* environment values are visible to the browser
- VITE_API_KEY is intentionally public
- participant and organizer tokens must never be mixed
- API-key 401 errors are different from expired Bearer-token 401 errors
- do not log out a user merely because the API key is misconfigured
- preserve Lovable visual quality while replacing mocks
- old Next.js prompts may contain stale API endpoint assumptions
- `AGENTS.md` is a stub pointing at `.agent`; do not restore the old Event Spark / Supabase map
- `WORKSPACE_STATE.md` is the cross-agent product/stage briefing; do not treat it as a substitute for this file's API contracts
- do not recreate `supabase/` or reinstall `@supabase/supabase-js`
- `README.md` still advertises HMAC-SHA256 as old PRD copy; not implemented and must not be rebuilt
- default git branch is `main`; GitHub Actions also listens to `master`
- Vite HMR can fail with `ENOTEMPTY` on `node_modules/.vite/deps` after lockfile/.env changes on Windows; restart `pnpm dev`
- `/` is public; do not auto-redirect logged-in participants away from Home
- Home, Browse, event detail, My Tickets, and shared house chrome use a tighter display scale (page titles `text-2xl`, catalog titles `text-sm`, event-detail hero ~24–34px, buttons default `h-10`). Do not restore `text-5xl`/`text-7xl` heroes, an in-hero white section pill, or a featured Home listing.
- Theme is `next-themes` class strategy (`app-theme`). House and organizer follow `html.dark`. Do not light-lock `.house-page` or `.org-console`. Public `/events/:id` (`.pulse-event`) stays light. QR pads stay `bg-white`. Dark console keeps teal brand; do not switch to generic slate/purple.
- Organizer console icons come from `orgIcons.ts` (Heroicons 2 / `react-icons/hi2`). Do not drop lucide glyphs back into organizer chrome, studio panels, or check-in. `Loader2` is the spinner exception. Only re-export names that exist in this `react-icons` build — a missing named export (`HiOutlineKeyboard`) blanks every route because `OrganizerLayout` is eagerly imported by `App.tsx`.
- Event Studio desktop uses a sticky section rail and native document scroll. Do not viewport-lock studio (`h-[100dvh] overflow-hidden`) — that nested `overflow-y-auto` plus Lenis made the wheel/touchpad dead (only dragging the scrollbar worked) and clipped Finance/Settings. Lenis stays off on `/organizer`.
- Do not set `overflow-x: hidden` on both `html` and `body`. That creates a second scrollport and clips wide children (tabs, tables, datetime inputs) so a phone viewport only shows the left half of the page. Shells use `overflow-x: clip`; horizontal regions use `.h-scroll` (bounded `overflow-x: auto`). Studio mobile tabs (`OrgStudioMobileNav`) must scroll inside a width-bounded scroller — never let `min-w-max` widen the page.
- Check-in unlock on `/organizer/scanner` is a centered `max-w-md` card, not a left-aligned form.
- Auth cards are `max-w-sm` with `h-10` controls. Do not restore a second `Logo size="lg"` on `/auth`.
- `SiteFooter` is a mist multi-column house footer (brand, Platform, Account, New listings). Used on Home, Browse, Auth, participant layout, and public event detail. On `/events/:id` it is light-locked via `.pulse-event .house-page` even when `html.dark`. No circular Search / Ticket / Organizer icons. Newsletter email is `localStorage` only (`event24.newsletter-email`); Laravel has no digest/subscribe route. No fake social networks or Privacy/Terms routes.
- participant login destination is `/` (Home). `/dashboard` still opens My Tickets. Never `/organizer/events`
- organizer login destination is `/organizer/dashboard`
- logging out organizer clears `organizer_token` only; participant session stays
- logging out participant clears `participant_token` only; organizer session stays
- `OrganizerProtectedRoute` is the organizer guard; `/organizer/login` and `/organizer/register` are public
- organizer event studio must not PATCH `status`, `featured`, `monetized`, or `organizer_id`
- event status changes only via `POST /organizer/events/{id}/transition` using EventStatusMachine targets
- other organizers' events return 404 "Event not found"; UI must show "You don't have access to this event." and must not render leaked details
- create quota failures are 403 with package messages; link organizers to `/organizer/subscription` for self-serve subscribe/upgrade (Prompt 15 backend + Web UI)
- gallery upload field name is `image`; jpeg/png/jpg/gif/webp; max 4096 KB
- **Custom registration form fields removed from product.** Web App join is ticket-only. Laravel endpoints `GET/POST …/form-fields` are gone. Table `event_form_fields` is **dropped**. Admin Event hub has no Form Fields tab (rebuild Admin if a stale build still shows it). `ParticipationService::join()` ignores answers. Legacy `participations.custom_field_answers` column may remain.
- **No waitlist.** Full events return 400 `Event capacity reached` (sold-out toast on Register). There is no promote route. `waitlisted` may appear on old rows only.
- **Capacity:** displayed registered = free joined + paid + checked-in. Unpaid pending **holds** a seat (`seats_remaining`) so checkout cannot oversell, but does **not** increment `registrations_count`. Waafi failure or pending expiry **cancels** the participation and releases ticket quantity; retry is a new join, not the cancelled row.
- ticket type delete is soft trash even when quantity_sold > 0
- `sales_enabled=false` means sales paused (ticket still exists) — not sold out. Organizer UI must say "Sales enabled" / "Sales paused" with the participant-facing explanation. Public registration filters those tickets out via `adaptTicketTypes`.
- Participant discount quote: `POST /participant/events/{event}/discount-codes/validate` body `{ code, ticket_type_id }` → `{ code, type, value, original_amount, discount_amount, final_amount }`. Join may include `discount_code`. Waafi / join charge uses snapshotted `final_amount` (display that amount; do not invent client-side pricing).
- VIP is only `ticket_types.is_vip === true` (default false). Never infer from ticket `name`. Organizer create/update send `is_vip`; public adapter and participant picker read that flag only.
- Event Studio overview (and settings capacity/deadline) uses local draft state + explicit **Save changes**. Do not PATCH on every blur/select — especially `event_mode` without `online_url` (422 for online/hybrid). Cover upload via `POST …/banner` may still save immediately.
- organizer create/update must send `event_mode`; `online_url` is required for `online` and `hybrid`. Do not invent a venue requirement for online-only events. `why_attend` is a max-6 string array — public Why Attend must use that list, never hardcoded marketing bullets. Map `event_mode` onto cinematic `location_type` (`in_person`→physical, `hybrid`→hybrid, `online`→virtual).
- invitation system templates expose `default_overlay_positions`, `default_customizations`, `thumbnail_path`, `background_image_path`. Participant `invitation.system_template` is the Eloquent model with those fields — normalize to overlay_positions / preview_image_path before drawing. Do not send `background_image_path` on invitation upsert; upload uses multipart field `background` (jpeg/png/jpg/webp, max 5120 KB). Canvas is locked 800×1100 portrait. Overlay x/y/width/height must be stored in that logical space (`screenPointToLogical` from the displayed preview box), never CSS/screen pixels. Save only schema fields (`sanitizeOverlayPositions` / `sanitizeCustomizations`). There is no invitation delete/reset or PDF compositing endpoint; reset PATCHes Laravel default overlay/customization objects. Mobile designer is preview-only.

## Agent Behavior Rules

1. Read `.agent` fully before coding.
2. Inspect existing code before creating alternatives.
3. Preserve Lovable UI unless the current prompt explicitly requests a redesign.
4. Never restore Supabase.
5. Never introduce HMAC.
6. Never invent Laravel API contracts.
7. Keep participant and organizer sessions separate.
8. Use environment configuration for all backend URLs/keys.
9. Update `.agent` in the same session as every meaningful change.
10. Work is incomplete until code and `.agent` agree.

## Update Protocol

For every meaningful change:

1. Update Last updated date + summary.
2. Update affected living sections.
3. Update Module Inventory if module status/data source changed.
4. Update routes if routing changed.
5. Update API contracts if a real contract was confirmed.
6. Append a detailed Change Log entry.
7. Self-check: can a new agent continue from `.agent` alone?

## Participant Registration + Payment API Contracts Confirmed

All under `/api/v1`. Header `X-API-Key` + Bearer `participant_token`.

- `POST /participant/events/{event}/discount-codes/validate` — body `{ code, ticket_type_id }`. Ticket must belong to the event and have `sales_enabled=true`. Success data: `{ code, type, value, original_amount, discount_amount, final_amount }` (amounts as `12.34` strings). 404 `discount_not_valid_for_event` / ticket not found; 400 `discount_inactive` | `discount_expired` | `discount_usage_exhausted`. Service: `src/services/participantDiscounts.ts`.
- `POST /participant/participations` — body `{ event_id, ticket_type_id?, discount_code? }`. Never send `user_id` or `custom_field_answers`. Returns wrapped `{ success, data: Participation }` (201). Participation may include `original_amount`, `discount_amount`, `final_amount` when a code was applied. Possible errors: 422 validation, 400 "already has an active participation", 400 "Registration deadline has passed", 400 "Invalid ticket type", 400 "Ticket type sales are disabled", 400 "Ticket type quantity exhausted", 400 "Event capacity reached", 400 discount_* codes.
  - `participation.status` values: `joined | paid | checked_in | cancelled` (`waitlisted` is legacy only; join never creates it)
  - `participation.payment_status` values: `not_required | pending | paid | refunded | failed`
  - Free or no-ticket → `payment_status=not_required`, `status=joined` → occupies a confirmed seat → navigate to event room
  - Paid ticket → `payment_status=pending`, `status=joined` → **does not occupy confirmed `registrations_count`**; still holds a seat so the event cannot be oversold until pay/fail/expire → WaafiPay
  - Discount to $0 → `payment_status=paid` (no Waafi) → occupies a confirmed seat
  - Capacity full → **400 Event capacity reached** (no waitlist)
  - Waafi **failure** or pending **expiry** → participation **cancelled**, ticket quantity released, seat freed; user may join again

- `POST /participant/payments/charge` — body `{ participation_id, payer_phone }`. Returns wrapped `{ success, data: Payment }`. Uses **210-second Axios timeout** (WaafiPay holds connection up to 180s). Backend charges snapshotted `final_amount` (not a client-invented amount). `payment.status` values: `pending | completed | refunded | failed`. On failure: `failure_code` + `failure_reason`. Error 400 "A payment is already pending" = idempotency guard. Error 400 "already paid" = race win, re-fetch participation. **Web client:** while charging, polls `GET /participant/participations/{id}` every 4s; treats `payment_status=paid|not_required` as success even if charge HTTP is still open, returns `pending`, or times out.

- `GET /participant/participations/{id}` — returns wrapped `{ success, data: Participation }` with `event` + `ticketType` relationships. Used both by Ticket page and as fallback re-check after charge.

## Participant Dashboard + Invitation API Contracts Confirmed

All under `/api/v1`. Header `X-API-Key` + Bearer `participant_token`.

- `GET /participant/participations` — paginated list. Response: `{ success, data: { items: Participation[], pagination: { current_page, last_page, per_page, total } } }`. Query params: `status`, `per_page`, `page`. Each item includes `event` + `ticketType` relations.
- `GET /participant/participations/{id}/invitation` — full invitation payload. Response: `{ success, data: { id, status, payment_status, qr_token, created_at, event, ticket_type, invitation, canvas: { width: 800, height: 1100 } } }`. `invitation` is null when the organizer has not configured a template. `invitation.mode` is `"template"` or `"custom"`. `invitation.overlay_positions` maps field names to `{ x, y, width?, height?, font_size?, font_color? }`. `invitation.background_image_path` is relative; pass through `getMediaUrl`.

## Participant Feedback + Certificate API Contracts Confirmed

All under `/api/v1`. Header `X-API-Key` + Bearer `participant_token`.

- `GET /participant/participations/{id}/feedback` — returns `{ success, data: EventFeedback | null }`. Returns null if participant has not yet submitted feedback. Fields: `id, participation_id, rating (int 1-5), comment (string|null), hidden (bool), submitted_at`.
- `POST /participant/event-feedback` — body `{ participation_id, rating, comment? }`. Returns `{ success, data: EventFeedback }` (201). Backend rules: only checked_in status allowed; duplicate rejected with 400.
- `GET /participant/participations/{id}/certificate` — returns `{ success, data: { available: bool, certificate: null | { id, issued_at, file_path, file_url, verified } } }`. `available: false` = not yet issued (deferred — do not fake it on the frontend).

Certificate delivery is deferred: the participant has read-only access to certificate state. The Web App shows a "not yet issued" explanation when `available === false` and a download button when `available === true`. Participants cannot issue or re-issue their own certificates; the read endpoint is the only certificate surface exposed to the participant Web App.

## Organizer Auth + Dashboard API Contracts Confirmed

All under `/api/v1`. Header `X-API-Key` always.

Public (`publicApi`, no Bearer):

- `POST /organizer-auth/register` — body `business_name`, `contact_name`, `email`, `phone?`, `password`, `password_confirmation`. Creates Organizer with `status=active`. Returns `{ success, data: { organizer, token, token_ability: organizer-web } }` (201). Token issued immediately; no email verification.
- `POST /organizer-auth/login` — body `email`, `password`. Success: same token envelope. Invalid credentials → 401. Suspended organizer → 403 `{ message, errors: { error_code: ["organizer_suspended"] } }`.

Authenticated (`organizerApi`, Bearer `organizer_token`):

- `GET /organizer-auth/me` — `{ success, data: { organizer } }`
- `POST /organizer-auth/logout` — current organizer token only; does not touch `participant_token`
- `PATCH /organizer-auth/profile` — `business_name`, `contact_name`, `email`, `phone`. Status not writable.
- `POST /organizer-auth/change-password` — `current_password`, `password`, `password_confirmation` (not `new_password`)
- `GET /organizer/dashboard` — `{ success, data: { organizer, active_subscription, total_events, total_registrations, total_revenue, available_payout, pending_payout, recent_events, quota? } }`. `quota` is omitted when there is no package. Quota shape: `{ quota, unlimited, zero_quota, events_created, can_create_event, remaining }`.

Organizer payload: `{ id, business_name, contact_name, email, phone, status }`.

## Organizer Events API Contracts Confirmed

All under `/api/v1`, `organizerApi` (X-API-Key + Bearer `organizer_token`). Owned events only.

- `GET /organizer/events` — query `status`, `search` (aliased to `q`), `q`, `per_page` (max 100), `page`. Searchable: `title`, `city`. Sort: `id|title|status|starts_at|created_at`. Index eager-loads `category` only. Envelope `{ success, data: { items, pagination } }`.
- `POST /organizer/events` — writable: `event_category_id`/`category_id`, `title` (required), `description`, `why_attend` (nullable string array, max 6, each max 200), `event_mode` (required: `in_person`|`online`|`hybrid`), `online_url` (required when mode is online or hybrid; url max 500), `city`, `address`, `latitude`, `longitude` (pair), `banner_path`, `capacity`, `registration_deadline`, `starts_at`, `ends_at`. Online events do not require city/address. Backend forces `status=draft`, `featured=false`, `monetized=false`, `organizer_id` from token. Do not send those overrides. Quota 403 messages: no active package; package quota 0; quota reached.
- `GET /organizer/events/{id}` — 404 `"Event not found"` if not owned (no 403 leak). Loads `category`, `images`, `ticketTypes`. Includes `event_mode`, `online_url`, `why_attend`.
- `PATCH /organizer/events/{id}` — same writable fields (`sometimes`). Rejects `status` (must use transition). Rejects `featured`, `monetized`, `organizer_id`. `online_url` required when the resulting mode is online/hybrid.
- `DELETE /organizer/events/{id}` — soft delete; `"Event moved to trash"`.
- `POST /organizer/events/{id}/transition` — `{ status }`. Returns `{ event, allowed_transitions }`. Invalid → 400 `invalid_status_transition`.
- Status machine: draft→published|cancelled; published→registration_open|draft|cancelled; registration_open→sold_out|registration_closed|ongoing|cancelled; sold_out→registration_closed|ongoing|cancelled; registration_closed→ongoing|cancelled; ongoing→completed|cancelled; completed/cancelled terminal.
- Banner/cover: `POST /organizer/events/{id}/banner` — multipart field **`banner`** (jpeg/png/jpg/gif/webp, max 4096 KB). Stores under `public/assets/images/events/` as `/assets/images/events/banner-{id}-…`. Response event includes `banner_path` + `banner_url` (absolute). Do **not** set cover via gallery `POST …/images` + `PATCH banner_path`. Clearing cover may still `PATCH` `banner_path: null`.
- Gallery: `GET /organizer/events/{id}/images`; `POST` multipart field `image` (jpeg/png/jpg/gif/webp, max 4096 KB); `DELETE /organizer/events/{id}/images/{image}`. Stored `assets/images/events/`. Gallery is separate from the event cover.

## Organizer Event Studio Architecture

Keep one EventDetail layout (Lovable header + EventSideNav). Nested React Router routes share that shell via `<Outlet />` and `EventStudioContext`. Do not split into six unrelated pages.

Documented paths (all under OrganizerLayout):

- `/organizer/events/:id` overview
- `/organizer/events/:id/tickets`
- `/organizer/events/:id/form`
- `/organizer/events/:id/content`
- `/organizer/events/:id/branding` and `/invitation` → overview (invitation designer removed)
- `/organizer/events/:id/attendees` (registrations + announcements)
- `/organizer/events/:id/lucky-wheel` (random winner picker + spin history)
- `/organizer/events/:id/scanner` (QR check-in; `/checkin` redirects here)
- `/organizer/events/:id/finance` (shared EventFinancePanel)
- `/organizer/events/:id/settings` (capacity / deadline / delete)
- `/organizer/events/:id/promotion` → redirects to overview (permanently removed)

Studio **section** sidebar groups (`OrgStudioNav`): EVENT (Overview, Tickets, Program), PEOPLE (Attendees, Check-in, Lucky wheel), MANAGE (Finance, Settings). Analytics stays routed, not in the rail. No Invitation/branding item. This rail is not app nav. Desktop rail is `sticky top-16` with 12px items; the page scrolls natively.

Reusable UI lives in `src/components/event-studio/` (`TicketTypeCard`, `TicketTypeForm`, `DiscountCodeForm`, `SpeakerCard`, `SpeakerForm`, `SponsorCard`, `SponsorForm`, `SessionTimeline`, `SessionForm`, `EventRegistrationsPanel`, `AnnouncementsPanel`, `LuckyWheelPanel`, `EventFinancePanel`, `SubscriptionQuotaPanel`). Scanner UI: `src/components/event-detail/CheckInScanner.tsx` via `EventStudioScanner`. Lucky wheel UI: `LuckyWheelPanel.tsx` via `EventStudioLuckyWheel`. Ticket UI is the static stub `PurchasedTicketStub` (QR + token only while claimable — hidden after check-in or event end). Download is a PNG of that pass (`src/lib/ticketImage.ts`) — not print-to-PDF.

Organizer chrome (`OrganizerLayout`): top bar with Dashboard, Events, Check-in, Finance. Settings in the avatar menu only. Org Attendees/Analytics URLs redirect into Events / studio analytics.

## Organizer Event Studio API Contracts Confirmed

Tickets (`organizerApi`):

- `GET /organizer/events/{id}/ticket-types` — `{ event_id, monetized, derived_monetized, ticket_types }`. Ticket type fields: `id`, `name`, `is_vip` (boolean, default false), `price`, `quantity_limit`, `quantity_sold`, `sort_order`, `sales_enabled`. VIP is never inferred from `name`.
- `POST /organizer/events/{id}/ticket-types` — `name`, `price` (required), `is_vip?` (defaults false), `quantity_limit?`, `sort_order?`, `sales_enabled?`. `quantity_sold` forced 0.
- `PATCH /organizer/ticket-types/{id}` — name/is_vip/price/quantity_limit/sales_enabled/sort_order
- `PATCH /organizer/ticket-types/{id}/sales` — `{ sales_enabled }`
- `DELETE /organizer/ticket-types/{id}` — soft delete (`Ticket type moved to trash`)

Discounts:

- `GET /organizer/events/{id}/discount-codes` — event-scoped plus organizer-wide (`event_id` null)
- `POST /organizer/events/{id}/discount-codes` — `code` (uppercased server-side), `type` (`percent`|`fixed`), `value`, `usage_limit?`, `expires_at?`, `active?`. Percent max 100.
- `PATCH /organizer/discount-codes/{id}`
- `PATCH /organizer/discount-codes/{id}/active` — `{ active }`
- `DELETE /organizer/discount-codes/{id}`

Speakers / sponsors / sessions (list envelope `{ items, pagination }`):

- Speakers: `GET/POST /organizer/events/{id}/speakers`, `PATCH/DELETE /organizer/speakers/{id}` — name required. Photo: multipart field `photo` on create, or `POST /organizer/speakers/{id}/photo` (jpeg/png/jpg/gif/webp, max 4096 KB). Stored `/assets/images/events/speakers/…`. Response includes `photo_path` + `photo_url`. Clearing photo: `PATCH` `photo_path: null`. Do not use a URL text field in studio.
- Sponsors: `GET/POST /organizer/events/{id}/sponsors`, `PATCH/DELETE /organizer/sponsors/{id}` — `tier` platinum|gold|silver|partner
- Sessions: `GET/POST /organizer/events/{id}/sessions`, `PATCH/DELETE /organizer/sessions/{id}` — title + starts_at required; speaker_id optional; no reorder endpoint

## Organizer Invitation API Contracts Confirmed

All under `/api/v1`, `organizerApi` (X-API-Key + Bearer `organizer_token`). Owned events only. Canvas: `App\Support\InvitationCanvas` 800×1100 portrait.

- `GET /organizer/invitation-system-templates` — active catalog: `id, name, slug, thumbnail_path, background_image_path, default_overlay_positions, default_customizations`
- `GET /organizer/events/{event}/invitation-template` — `{ event_id, template, canvas }`. `template` may be null.
- `POST /organizer/events/{event}/invitation-template` — create; `mode` required (`template`|`custom`); `system_template_id` required_if mode=template (active, not soft-deleted)
- `PATCH /organizer/events/{event}/invitation-template` — update same fields; do not send `background_image_path`
- `POST /organizer/events/{event}/invitation-template/background` — multipart field `background`; mimes jpeg/png/jpg/webp; max 5120 KB; stored `assets/images/events/invitations/`. If no row exists, creates with `mode=custom` + default overlays/customizations.

Default overlay keys: `qr_code`, `participant_name`, `event_title`, `event_date`, `event_time`, `event_venue`, `ticket_type`, `organizer_logo`. Default customizations: `primary_color`, `secondary_color`, `font_family`, `header_text` (optional `logo_path`).

Participant `GET /participant/participations/{id}/invitation` returns `invitation` as `{ mode, system_template (full model), background_image_path, customizations, overlay_positions }` or null → fallback gradient card.

Ownership: cross-organizer IDs return 404. UI uses `isOrganizerEventAccessError` → "You don't have access to this event."

## Organizer Registrations + Announcements + Analytics API Contracts Confirmed

All under `/api/v1`, `organizerApi` (X-API-Key + Bearer `organizer_token`). Owned events only. Services: `src/services/organizerParticipations.ts`, `organizerAnnouncements.ts`, `organizerAnalytics.ts`, `organizerLuckyWheel.ts`.

Participations (registrations):

- `GET /organizer/events/{id}/participations` — query `status?` (`joined|paid|checked_in|cancelled`), `per_page`, `page`. Envelope `{ success, data: { items, pagination, event_id, capacity } }`. Capacity: `{ registered_count` (confirmed seats only), `waitlisted_count` always `0`, `capacity`, `seats_remaining` from held seats }. Items include `user`, ticket as `ticket_type` and/or `ticketType`, `status`, `payment_status`, amounts, `created_at`.
- `GET /organizer/participations/{id}` — single row with `user`, `event`, ticket relation.
- `POST /organizer/participations/{id}/cancel` — body `{ reason? }` (`nullable|string|max:500`). Does **not** claim automatic refund. UI confirms strongly and states cancellation does not auto-refund. There is **no promote/waitlist** route.

Participation status enum: `joined | paid | checked_in | cancelled` (legacy `waitlisted` may exist in old rows). Payment status: `not_required | pending | paid | refunded | failed`. Confirmed seats (capacity display): free `joined` + `paid`/`checked_in`. Pending unpaid holds a seat for sold-out but is not counted in `registrations_count`. Failed payment cancels the row.

Lucky wheel:

- `GET /organizer/events/{id}/lucky-wheel` — `{ event_id, participant_count, participants[], attempts[] }`. Participants = confirmed-seat registrations only (free joined / paid / checked-in). **Pending unpaid, cancelled, and legacy waitlisted are excluded.**
- `POST /organizer/events/{id}/lucky-wheel/spin` — body `{ winner_count }` (required int ≥ 1, must be ≤ participant count). Randomly picks that many unique winners, stores `lucky_wheel_attempts` + `lucky_wheel_winners`. Returns attempt (201). 422 when no participants or winner count too high.

Announcements:

- `GET /organizer/events/{id}/announcements` — paginated `{ items, pagination }`. Fields: `id`, `event_id`, `subject`, `body`, `sent_at`, `sent_by`. UI treats history as sent/read-only.
- `POST /organizer/events/{id}/announcements` — `{ subject, body }` (required). Emails non-cancelled participants. Response message includes recipient count (shown in toast).

Analytics:

- `GET /organizer/events/{id}/analytics` — scalars only: `event_id`, `views`, `registrations`, `conversion_rate` (nullable), `revenue`, `currency`, `check_ins`, `attendance_rate` (nullable), `average_rating` (nullable), `feedback_count`. Do **not** invent time-series, funnel steps, or extra KPIs. Charts derive only from these returned numbers.

CSV: client-side export of the currently loaded/filtered page is allowed; UI labels “Export this page” and states it is not all results unless every page was fetched.

## Organizer Finance + Payouts + Package API Contracts Confirmed

All under `/api/v1`, `organizerApi` (X-API-Key + Bearer `organizer_token`). Services: `organizerFinance.ts`, `organizerPayouts.ts`, `organizerPackages.ts`.

Finance (owned event):

- `GET /organizer/events/{id}/finance` — `EventFinanceService::summary`: `{ event_id, currency, total_collected, total_paid_out, total_reserved, outstanding_balance }`. `total_collected` = completed (non-refunded) payments. `total_reserved` = sum of requested+approved+paid `requested_amount`. `outstanding_balance` = collected − reserved. **No refunds/net fields** — do not invent them. Note: after payout status `paid`, admin refunds may return `refund_blocked_payout_recorded`; UI does not promise automatic clawback.

Payouts (per-event only; no organizer-wide batch create):

- `GET /organizer/payout-requests` — paginated list for the authenticated organizer (`items`, `pagination`). Statuses: `requested|approved|paid|rejected`.
- `GET /organizer/events/{id}/payout-requests` — same list scoped to event + `{ event_finance, available_amount }` (`available_amount` = outstanding balance).
- `POST /organizer/events/{id}/payout-requests` — `{ requested_amount }` (required, min 0.01). Creates with status `requested` and **snapshotted** `commission_rate` from platform settings. `commission_amount` / `net_amount` may be null until admin approval. Amount > outstanding → 400.
- `GET /organizer/payout-requests/{id}` — `{ payout, snapshot_amounts: { commission_amount, net_amount }, event_finance, available_amount }`. Show `admin_notes` read-only when present.
- Do **not** wire Admin `approve` / `reject` / `record-payment`.

Packages (read-only — no purchase):

- `GET /organizer/packages` — active catalog: `id`, `name`, `description`, `price`, `event_quota`, `duration_value`, `duration_unit`, `duration_label`, `tier_rank`, `status`, plus lifecycle `is_current`, `selectable`, `upgrade_allowed`, `blocked_reason`, `action`
- `GET /organizer/subscription` — `{ active, history }` with snapshots / seconds_remaining / quota_usage
- `GET /organizer/quota` — EventQuota fields + `has_active_subscription` + package summary + subscription timing
- `POST /organizer/subscriptions` — body `{ package_id, payer_phone? }` only (backend Prompt 15; Web UI not wired yet)
- `GET /organizer/subscriptions/history`, `GET /organizer/subscription-orders`, `GET /organizer/subscription-orders/{id}`

UI: one shared `EventFinancePanel` for Event Studio Finance tab and `/organizer/payouts` event tab. `/organizer/payouts` package tab embeds compact `SubscriptionQuotaPanel`; full Plans & billing is `/organizer/subscription`.

## Organizer QR Check-In API Contracts Confirmed

Organizer-authenticated scanner (`organizerApi` + Bearer `organizer_token`). Service: `src/services/organizerQr.ts`.

- `POST /organizer/scanner/unlock` — body `{ scan_token }` → `{ event_id, title, status, event_mode }` for owned events only.
- `POST /organizer/qr-scan-logs/validate` — body `{ token, gate?, event_id? }`. When `event_id` is set, tickets from other events are `INVALID`. Response includes `result` (`valid` | `already_used` | `invalid`), `checked_in`, `participation`, `scan_log`.
- `GET /organizer/events/{id}/qr-scan-logs` — `{ event_id, stats, scan_logs }`
- `GET /organizer/events/{id}/check-in-stats` — door stats

Routes: **organizer nav** `/organizer/scanner` (logged-in, token unlock) and studio `/organizer/events/:id/scanner`.

## Public door scanner (`/qrscan`)

No login — API-key only + event `scan_token`. Service: `src/services/publicQr.ts`. Page: `PublicQrScanPage.tsx` at **`/qrscan`**. **Not linked** from marketing home nav; door staff use the URL directly.

- `POST /public/scanner/unlock` — `{ scan_token }` → `{ event_id, title, status, event_mode }`
- `POST /public/qr-scan-logs/validate` — `{ scan_token, token, gate?, event_id? }` (same result shape as organizer validate)
- `POST /public/scanner/events/{id}/qr-scan-logs` — body `{ scan_token }` → `{ event_id, stats, scan_logs }`

`CheckInScanner` accepts optional `scanToken` prop to call public endpoints instead of organizer ones.

Event `scan_token` is generated on create; organizer show/update/banner/transition JSON includes it (`makeVisible`). Studio Settings maps `scan_token` through `toStudioEvent` and Copy; missing tokens are backfilled on GET and can use **Generate token**. Online events: invitation omits door `qr_token`.

## Participant event room + discussions

- `GET /participant/participations/{id}/announcements`
- `GET|POST /participant/events/{event}/discussions` (+ PATCH/DELETE own)
- Organizer: `GET /organizer/events/{event}/discussions?speaker_id=`, `PATCH .../answered`
- Organizer: `GET /organizer/events/{event}/feedback` (attendee feedback list)
- Feedback submit allowed after event `ends_at` past or status `completed` (not check-in-only)
- Public `online_url` is hidden; registered participants see it on invitation/event room

## Change Log

### 2026-09-05 — Vercel static SPA deploy config

Added `vercel.json` (Vite, `pnpm install` / `pnpm build`, output `dist`, SPA rewrite to `index.html`) and `packageManager: pnpm@10.12.4` so Vercel does not pick leftover `package-lock.json`. `.vercel` is gitignored. Production must set `VITE_API_BASE_URL` + `VITE_API_KEY` on Vercel (build-time); localhost API will not work from the hosted site. After first URL: set `VITE_APP_URL`, allow the origin on Laravel CORS, add it to Google OAuth JS origins.

Files: `vercel.json`, `package.json`, `.gitignore`, `.agent`.

### 2026-09-05 — Product name Event24

The Web App product name is **Event24** (formerly EventHub). Fallback `VITE_APP_NAME` / `env.appName`, `index.html` titles, Logo fallback, pass copy (`Event24 pass · E24-xxxxx`), PNG download `event24-pass-…`, newsletter/session/studio storage keys (`event24.*`), package.json `name`, docs, Cursor rules, and design exports all use Event24. Disk paths under `D:\Orbit Systems\EventHub\` are unchanged (folder name). Live wordmark still comes from `GET /platform/branding` when Admin has an organization name — update Admin Settings → Organization to Event24 or the API name will keep winning.

Files: `src/lib/env.ts`, `src/lib/ticketImage.ts`, `src/lib/authStorage.ts`, `src/lib/lastStudioEvent.ts`, `src/components/participant/PurchasedTicketStub.tsx`, `src/components/layout/SiteFooter.tsx`, `src/pages/RegistrationDetail.tsx`, `index.html`, `package.json`, `.env.example`, `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `design/MASTER.md`, `design/design-system.pen`, `design/export/organizer.html`, `design/export/organizer-mobile.html`, `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`, `check-agent-update.sh`, `install-agent-hook.*`, `.github/workflows/agent-context-check.yml`, `.agent`.

### 2026-09-05 — Human product briefing (`PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`)

Added a standalone project-context markdown at the repo root for marketers and newcomers. It describes the live Event24 Web App (catalog → in-page register → My Tickets → door / room; organizer studio, Waafi, plans, payouts), the house / venue / org-console split, locked CTAs, and what not to claim. Leftover Lovable README fiction is called out as non-authoritative. Engineering truth is unchanged and stays in this `.agent` file.

Files: `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`, `.agent`.

### 2026-09-03 — Pending registration: resume main checkout UI

`/registrations/:id` with `payment_status=pending|failed` now renders `CheckoutLayout` + `WaafiPayStep` (same as in-event checkout) instead of a locked stub + standalone Waafi card. Loads `GET /participant/participations/{id}` for snapshotted `final_amount` / discount totals via `participationCheckoutPricing`.

Files: `RegistrationDetail.tsx`, `participationCheckout.ts`, `.agent`.

### 2026-09-03 — My Tickets: hide unpaid pending registrations

`/dashboard/home` (My Tickets) lists only purchased tickets (`payment_status` paid or not_required, not cancelled/waitlisted). Pending checkout rows stay on `/registrations/:id` for payment completion but no longer appear in the ticket list. Register cancel copy updated accordingly.

Files: `AttendeeHome.tsx`, `nextEvent.ts`, `Register.tsx`, `.agent`.

### 2026-09-03 — App-wide dark mode status badges + scanner buttons

Centralized theme-safe status pills in `src/lib/statusBadges.ts` + `StatusBadge` component. Participant pages (registration, My Tickets), organizer attendees table, and lucky wheel use shared badge classes with explicit `dark:` text colors. Check-in scanner white buttons use `orgOnWhiteBtnClass` (fixed dark ink) instead of `text-oc-ink`, which flips to near-white in dark mode and made **Start camera** / **Scan next** invisible.

Files: `statusBadges.ts`, `StatusBadge.tsx`, `CheckInScanner.tsx`, `RegistrationDetail.tsx`, `EventRegistrationsPanel.tsx`, `LuckyWheelPanel.tsx`, `AttendeeHome.tsx`, `PurchasedTicketStub.tsx`, `orgTheme.ts`, `badge.tsx`, `.agent`.

